A rejected change to the model test's timing bound, kept so the next attempt starts from it.

Written on 2026-11-27, with no spec, against 71fb3b9c, by the session that narrowed the open item
*Two timing tests fail* in docs/architecture.md §12, which records why it was not landed. It put
the bound on a call's "own time": elapsed, less an excuse read from each thread's schedstat around
the call, the lesser of the longest any one thread waited for a CPU and what the calling thread
itself could have lost, capped at one EPSILON. Its second diff review found that the kernel it was
measured on counts a sleeping thread's sleep as waiting for a CPU often enough to excuse a plain
stall and to fail two of this patch's own tests under load (timing_bound_schedstat_sleep.py beside
this file). Only the three test files are here; its docs are not. `git apply` skips this note.

