+    ``switch_interval`` for each time it was given one, since a thread waiting for the
+    interpreter lock sleeps at most that long before it wakes to ask again. The first alone
+    excuses a caller that is blocked for a real reason while an unrelated thread is starved,
+    which a review reproduced on an idle machine with two threads sharing a CPU. The second
+    alone is the remedy first proposed and does not bind: under the interpreter lock a caller
+    waits blocked, which the kernel does not count, behind a holder that is runnable and not
+    running, and a reproduced failure of 1.263 s had 0.8 ms of its own wait.
